 "description": "Schokker2013 - A mathematical model representing cellular immune development and response to Salmonella of chicken intestinal tissue\nBioModels BIOMD0000000895 (curated). SBML file: Schokker2013.xml.\nSimulation: 0 to 40 time units (SED-ML: Schokker2013.sedml), sampling 0.04.\nRun switches: -ig:mass -INT:1 -obeymaxint\nVerification against libRoadRunner (SBML reference): PASS, max |difference| = 4.66e-06 of species peak (worst: Mi)\nSBML time units are used unchanged as Kintecus seconds.\nConversion notes:\n  [info] Mr_Infection: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] CD4_Growth_Boost term 2/2: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] CD8_Growth_Boost term 2/2: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] Mi_Bursting: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] Mi_Lysis term 1/4: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] Mi_Lysis term 2/4: rate order differs from the stoichiometry; consumed on separate line(s) - Mi: zero order, signed\n  [info] Si_Proliferation term 2/2: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] Mi_Lysis_Si: rate not proportional to its reactants; written once as signed lines (source+S[USER;...]) for Si",
